{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 33","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_33\">Problem 33</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 33\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/c/97c0ed623813f94ea0708a5f7477c242e440cc51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\dfrac{3}{4}x + 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> and a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to the given line and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units from it. A possible equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7dce355ce5600fb95fbf21fdbdd763690410a16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ y =\\frac{3}{4}x+1\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ y =\\frac{3}{4}x\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ y =\\frac{3}{4}x-\\frac{2}{3}\\qquad  \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ y = \\dfrac{3}{4}x -1 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ y = \\dfrac{3}{4}x + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"406\" height=\"76\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/b/0abbcdea7ca5786a4d6d6989210d9e07e41c1093.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  import graph; size(8.22 cm); real lsf=0.5; pen dps=linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10); defaultpen(dps); pen ds=black; real xmin=-10.2,xmax=10.2,ymin=-10.2,ymax=10.2;  pen cqcqcq=rgb(0.75,0.75,0.75), evevff=rgb(0.9,0.9,1), zzttqq=rgb(0.6,0.2,0);   /*grid*/ pen gs=linewidth(0.7)+cqcqcq+linetype(&quot;2 2&quot;); real gx=1,gy=1; for(real i=ceil(xmin/gx)*gx;i&lt;=floor(xmax/gx)*gx;i+=gx) draw((i,ymin)--(i,ymax),gs); for(real i=ceil(ymin/gy)*gy;i&lt;=floor(ymax/gy)*gy;i+=gy) draw((xmin,i)--(xmax,i),gs);  Label laxis; laxis.p=fontsize(10);  xaxis(xmin,xmax,defaultpen+black,Ticks(laxis,Step=1.0,Size=2,NoZero),Arrows(6),above=true); yaxis(ymin,ymax,defaultpen+black,Ticks(laxis,Step=1.0,Size=2,NoZero),Arrows(6),above=true); clip((xmin,ymin)--(xmin,ymax)--(xmax,ymax)--(xmax,ymin)--cycle);  draw((16/3,10)--(-10,-3/2),Arrows); dot((12/5,14/5)); dot((0,6)); draw((0,6)--(12/5,14/5),dotted);  [/asy]\" width=\"392\" height=\"392\" />\n</p><p>If a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is four units away from another line, the perpendicular distance between the two lines is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Since a line perpendicular to the original has a slope of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093dd6ce333d2352545ecd4c64e68be42a536722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\tfrac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"23\" height=\"21\" />, a point on that line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/7/7a7dab1b6e7f8f74319e4b848e6b0cd434c72007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> units away and can be derived from subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8fba9005cb63bba4318f8b13049aa3006547cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from the y-coordinate and adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b26c8398882a95a9099c7b9516439dd6b467c65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3d$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" /> to the x-coordinate of a point on the original line.\n</p><p>We want the perpendicular distance to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a1025e78542df081d3736265712109b94857821e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\tfrac{4}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"46\" height=\"23\" />.  Since one point on the original line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db195dda1786b430841585b3b552cfeeeca0f6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, a point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcaf639c0a614c820fb51f5fa2ce5f13eb0232a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0+3 \\cdot \\tfrac{4}{5},6 - 4 \\cdot \\tfrac{4}{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"149\" height=\"21\" />, which is simplified as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bbb2b69c601a58d838dbf51eb6130d1259624a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\tfrac{12}{5},\\tfrac{14}{5})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"55\" height=\"21\" />.  Using point-slope form, the equation of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4e07a424bf9260fb7231af731cd78c6b23cbcf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y - \\frac{14}{5} = \\frac{3}{4} (x - \\frac{12}{5})\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb8fdf77ebc09b9809d7d18c4671c8993fad46ba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac{3}{4} x + 1\\]\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 32\">Problem 32</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%